<section class="visit-process" aria-labelledby="visit-process-title">
  <div class="process-inner">
    <p class="process-eyebrow">Our leak detection visit</p>
    <h2 id="visit-process-title">How Atlanta Leak Detection Works</h2>
    <p class="process-intro">Most residential leak detection appointments run 60 to 90 minutes from arrival to written report. A buried supply line that runs from the meter to the house can take longer, and commercial systems with larger pipe networks longer still. We'll give you a realistic time estimate when we book so you can plan your day.</p>

    <ol class="process-steps">
      <li class="process-step">
        <span class="step-marker" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <h3>Inspect</h3>
        <p>A full property walkthrough, a review of your water bill history, and a pressure check to narrow down where the leak is coming from.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="process-step">
        <span class="step-marker" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <h3>Locate</h3>
        <p>Thermal imaging and Aquaphon A200 acoustic detection pinpoint the exact location of the leak, with no demolition required.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="process-step">
        <span class="step-marker" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
        <h3>Report</h3>
        <p>You get a written report on what we found and a separate written estimate before any work starts. No pressure to commit on the spot.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="process-step">
        <span class="step-marker" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
        <h3>Repair</h3>
        <p>Our licensed plumbers fix the leak the same day when possible, opening only the one spot we confirmed.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

